course: dictionary
lesson: 10138
title: Thrifty and money words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thrifty person is careful with money and does not waste things. They save, reuse and buy only what they need. Thrifty is an adjective, so it describes a person or a habit: «thrifty shopper», «thrifty habits». Its other forms are thriftier and thriftiest.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Saving pocket money, comparing prices and mending things all suggest thrifty. Ask yourself what word would fit in the sentence, then put thrifty in its place and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Thrifty can also describe something that is not about money. «A two-toed sloth hangs upside down from a branch and does not seem to move for an hour; it is not lazy but thrifty.» The sloth saves every bit of energy, so thrifty here means it does not waste energy.
fact: Thrifty means careful with money and not wasteful.
fact: Thrifty people save, reuse and buy only what they need.
fact: A «thrift store» in the USA is a charity shop that sells used items.
fact: In wartime, thrifty families «made do and mend», fixing things rather than throwing them away.
fact: «Thrifty» can describe a person, a habit, or a way of doing things, like the sloth saving energy.
exercise: «She is a thrifty shopper and always compares prices.» What does thrifty mean here? | Spending as much as she can | Happy and loud | Very quick at running | *Careful with money and not wasteful
exercise: In the USA, what is a «thrift store»? | A market for fresh food | *A charity shop selling used items | A shop that sells only new toys | A bank for saving pocket money
exercise: Which is a thrifty habit? | Buying everything you see | Losing your pocket money on the way home | Throwing things away as soon as they break | *Mending a torn coat instead of buying a new one
test: Which other forms does «thrifty» have? | thrifts and thrifting | more thrifty and most thrifty of all | thriftly and thriftest | *thriftier and thriftiest
test: Why is the sloth in the example described as thrifty? | *It saves every bit of energy by moving slowly | It buys its leaves from a shop | It never needs to sleep | It spends all its energy running fast
exam: Which sentence uses thrifty in a money sense? | *Ben saves his pocket money and buys second-hand books | Ben forgets where he left his coat | Ben runs faster than anyone in his class | Ben spends all his money on sweets at lunch
